    text: "Final local revision validation: packed npm/npx/bunx and SDK consumer smoke passes for version 2026.10.2 and nine package surfaces; package-first dogfood passes. Exact generated-report admission receipt test-local-murdgisu-s8759q passes and records the eight observed covered/total counts plus four percentages, bound to coverage-summary SHA-256 fa944974f43987bf88083321387a75a302312d9120632e28374a077304e8197c. The complete suite is executed once under test-local-murdbyvj-6ohpqa. Fresh unchanged-main CodSpeed baseline run 37055126994 succeeds on b52bb3b; revised-head performance comparison remains a hosted delivery check. Native merged-main Scorecard retirement and next eligible publication are explicitly tracked by open standing owner pm-7zs0."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T20:21:55.206Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Round-two TDD: the unchanged admission and shared secret policy failed six relevant assertions: nested node_modules/axios was admitted and five composed empty-fallback expressions evaded both scanners. Source-workspace alias controls independently failed. No gate or threshold is relaxed; repair complete-expression admission, reject dependency shadowing while retaining generated executable shims, and rebase included source aliases into the disposable workspace."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T20:24:18.275Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Second-head performance evidence: Chrome dashboard compares 32eff2c with b52bb3b and still reports 2.64 percent aggregate regression, six changed benchmarks and five unchanged. It explicitly shows AMD EPYC 9V45 96-Core baseline versus AMD EPYC 7763 64-Core head, differing instruction flags, and identical native build ID 574e1ea5495a22829428f4c8cc4bd474ffc7c710. CodSpeed documents that shared-runner CPU differences affect simulated cache behavior: https://codspeed.io/docs/instruments/cpu/regression-causes. The unchanged-main refresh succeeds but does not make this comparison equivalent. Native benchmark execution passes; causality and performance acceptance remain limited. No threshold, acknowledgment or paid runner is changed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T20:34:43.636Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "The revised focused boundary suites pass 44 tests across five files. A further real filesystem control replaced an approved bundle with a symlink to identical bytes and correctly failed before tightening admission. Owned artifacts now must be regular files, and nested module shadowing is rejected; generated .bin shims remain supported. Full static quality, typecheck, secret scanning and documentation links pass; focused lint and actual installed-package admission pass after the additional regular-file control. The complete canonical coverage run is next, with no source edits during execution."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T20:57:59.333Z"
