  - created_at: "2026-10-02T21:21:05.684Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final frozen-source canonical run test-local-murgv9bh-hqiwl4 passes 9616 tests across 762 suites, with two existing Windows-only skips. Exact statements 66428/66428, branches 50839/50839, functions 13732/13732 and lines 63349/63349 enforce unchanged 100/100/100/100. Report receipt test-local-murgvxx1-115b0n independently admits generated coverage-summary SHA-256 100c1ea48effbcab2948e31db190eefbdaa99501ba52ad22acb30b1521033bab and records all twelve actual count/percentage measurements without repeating the full suite. The real globally installed npm prerequisite is exposed through NODE_PATH; the packed continuation test and all regression controls remain unchanged. Typed verifies edges share this canonical proof with pm-5iwfkj and pm-iktual."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T21:22:14.740Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Focused owner-linked receipt test-local-murgwhe8-iio2d6 passes 44 cases across installed artifact corruption/shadow/symlink controls, real CJS/ESM loopback HTTP behavior, and native CI/release workflow contracts. The same source has the full canonical exact-count proof. Every actionable round-two inline finding has a specific implementation response and useful feedback vote; package publication and merged-main analyzer retirement remain independent delivery checks."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T21:29:10.077Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final local acceptance after all review fixes and the eligible MCP Apps refresh: packed npm/npx/bunx version 2026.10.2 and nine package surfaces pass, including a plain installed SDK TypeScript consumer. The 89-command package-first dogfood journey passes in a cleaned temporary tracker. Full dependency audit reports no known vulnerabilities, all twelve owned regular artifacts pass hash/inventory admission, secrets scan is clear, and documentation links pass. Optional live Ollama semantic dogfood was not requested and remains explicitly unattempted. Hosted exact-head review, native Windows, performance comparison and merged-main analyzer retirement remain independent checks."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T22:04:13.481Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Exact-head round 3: Greptile identified valid empty configuration fallbacks followed by comments being detected as literal passwords. Add shared SDK/repository positive and negative controls before admitting bounded comment suffixes; operators, concatenations and later credential literals must remain detectable. Cubic TOON complaint is a false positive: the second learning contains no commas and is correctly decoded by the canonical CLI and strict all-status/history validation."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T22:06:54.618Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Regression-first result: four benign commented configuration controls failed before implementation. The shared rule now accepts bounded trailing line/block comments, with the first block closing delimiter respected. Controls for continuation after line/block comments, credential literals between comments, chained OR, concatenation and composed ternaries stay detectable. All 39 shared policy cases and all 48 focused cases pass; no path exemption or test mock was added."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T22:08:38.573Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Exact-head performance observation at ab2c663: CodSpeed reports a 2.63 percent advisory across six benchmarks and explicitly flags different runtime environments. Chrome confirms base AMD EPYC 9V45 versus head AMD EPYC 7763, different AVX capabilities, unchanged native build ID 574e1ea5495a22829428f4c8cc4bd474ffc7c710 and fifteen unmeasured fingerprint system calls totalling 247.2 microseconds. The benchmarked source and native payload are unchanged. This supports comparison uncertainty, not a proven causal explanation or an equivalent-environment performance pass; no advisory acknowledgement, threshold change or paid runner was used."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T22:11:11.252Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: Independent review confirmed that JavaScript line comments also end at Unicode U+2028 and U+2029. The current trailing-comment class would swallow a continued operator/literal across those separators. Add both shared-consumer negative controls before restricting the class to all four JavaScript line terminators.
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T22:18:45.415Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final focused policy verification: all 42 shared-consumer cases pass, including benign trailing comments and Windows CRLF endings plus detection of ordinary and Unicode line continuations, literals between block comments, chained fallbacks and genuine credential classes. All 51 focused snapshot/CLI/policy cases pass. Canonical coverage will be rerun after serial static quality and typechecking on frozen source; previous full-run evidence remains historical rather than being reused for this new source revision."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T22:26:24.298Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Static validation retained its required thresholds and exposed cleared expected-result fields after canonical reopen. Restored explicit expectations through the PM CLI for the two active owners; the failing tracker assertion is preserved as evidence. The fresh live census shows zero open Dependabot alerts and zero open secret-scanning alerts; the sole historical secret alert is already classified false positive. Registry confirms CodSpeed 5.7.1, MCP Apps 2.0.3 and pm-changelog 2026.9.25 remain latest."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T22:37:46.797Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Full static quality and all four TypeScript projects pass after restoring active expected-result metadata. A real temporary scanner control closes the Trivy proof gap: official checksummed Trivy 0.70.0, matching hosted job 111039270530, scans pnpm lockfile 9.0 with include-dev-deps and current DB. A development-only Axios 1.4.0 fixture exits 1 with thirteen HIGH/CRITICAL findings; replacing only its dev dependency with Axios 1.20.0 exits 0 with zero HIGH/CRITICAL findings. Both temporary installations and the isolated downloaded binary were removed. This proves scanner behavior without seeding vulnerable dependencies in the repository or weakening native gates."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T23:02:54.506Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final source proof: canonical test-local-murk9e8z-r4gw2y passes 9628 tests across 762 suites with only the two existing Windows-only skips. Observed statements 66443/66443, branches 50848/50848, functions 13734/13734 and lines 63364/63364 are exact 100/100/100/100. Measured report test-local-murkhsbe-xcywcf records all twelve count/percentage values from coverage-summary SHA-256 f586fac52502b298f1401e44e92e9330eda233cdcd7bd05fd3f88e6de87d551c without repeating the suite. Shared parity receipt test-local-murkcofa-t7qfi3 passes 42 cases. Serial static/typecheck, real Trivy dev-negative/positive fixtures, final packed npm/npx/bunx SDK consumers and package-first dogfood pass. Native exact-head review, Windows and merged-main alert retirement remain separate required delivery boundaries."
  - created_at: "2026-10-03T00:12:19.199Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "The shared primary-owner verification is renewed for the final snapshot correction: canonical test-local-murmvdoi-pilgng passes 9629 tests and all four coverage percentages are exactly 100. Measured report test-local-murmxdfi-0nvqus retains twelve actual values, with covered/total statements 66459, branches 50854, functions 13736 and lines 63377, bound to SHA-256 413ae1baf7cba0ef38d7fa780999fd33ae2a32c769f73079bf4adb43b891d69b. Existing security behavior, full audit and twelve-artifact bundle inventory remain verified. Source ownership of the new dependency-alias and destination fixes remains pm-5iwfkj; its current closure references this shared proof. The earlier immutable security closure remains valid historical evidence. Native merged-main Scorecard retirement and publication remain independent under pm-7zs0."
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-02T06:37:50.731Z","harness:codex","Scope and evidence boundary: this intake documents an unresolved development-tool dependency report before merging PR1372. It is not a regression introduced by the scoped recovery, continuation or semantic-preview fixes. Production-only audit is clean. Full audit and native Scorecard remain open; embedded Axios requires separate inspection beyond pnpm lock resolution. Do not dismiss the scanner alert or report security clearance until remediation and native merged-main scans are verified."
  "2026-10-02T19:24:09.415Z","harness:codex","Large-patch review rationale: GitHub treats a new patch artifact as 38,448 added lines although the upstream diff removes 38,404 lines and adds ten. Only two bundles and their two maps change; three native payloads remain byte-identical. Replacing the patch with an upstream supported fixed release is preferable once one is available and passes the same inventory, runtime, map and native gates. The exact-version pnpm patch remains reproducible across frozen installs and does not introduce an install-time transformation or weaken dependency admission."
  "2026-10-02T22:37:47.608Z","harness:codex","Reproducible manual Trivy control: in a fresh temporary directory create a private package whose sole devDependency is axios 1.4.0, run pnpm install --lockfile-only --ignore-scripts, then the official checksummed 0.70.0 trivy filesystem --include-dev-deps --scanners vuln --severity HIGH,CRITICAL --exit-code 1 --format json on that directory. Expect exit 1 and detected Axios findings. Change the sole devDependency to axios 1.20.0, regenerate the lock and repeat; expect exit 0 and zero selected-severity findings. Observed archive SHA-256 8b4376d5d6befe5c24d503f10ff136d9e0c49f9127a4279fd110b727929a5aa9; lock format 9.0. The local comparison reused the current vulnerability database, and all temporary data was cleaned."
learnings[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-02T18:32:24.961Z","harness:codex","Externalizing an embedded HTTP client must preserve its isolation from application interceptors, not just its version and exported API. Dedicated Axios clients, real HTTP compatibility controls, reviewed map coordinates and immutable native hashes cover different risks; lockfile audit alone cannot detect an embedded obsolete implementation."
  "2026-10-02T20:36:49.766Z","harness:codex",Content hashes alone do not pin JavaScript resolution boundaries. An identical-byte bundle symlink or nested node_modules client can redirect imports; exact owned-file inventory plus regular-file admission covers that boundary. Public-expression secret exceptions must recognize complete expressions rather than prefixes and share the same controls across SDK and repository scanners.
  "2026-10-02T22:27:26.037Z","harness:codex","Expression exceptions must account for JavaScript comment delimiters and all four line terminators without consuming later code. Separate genuine acceptance controls from continued-expression detection controls in both SDK and repository consumers. Canonical reopening also clears prior terminal expectations; restate active expected behavior through the CLI before strict tracker validation, and retain failed attempts as evidence."
